{#-
  The image prompt frame (M3-03).

  Block ORDER is the point of this file, not the wording. The character's
  immutable traits come LAST, after the scene, because both diffusion models
  and instruction-following models weight the end of a prompt more heavily —
  so the one thing that must never drift is the last thing read. Reordering
  these blocks silently weakens character consistency (R7) while every test
  still passes, which is why the reasoning lives here rather than in a commit
  message.

  Blocks arrive pre-rendered. Scene text is never interpolated into the
  character block; see `image_prompt.build_image_prompt`.

  EVERY LINE HERE IS POSITIVE. Nothing in this file names a thing it does not
  want, because an image model reads the noun and not the instruction — the
  same rule that keeps `style.avoid` out of the positive block (`style.py`).
  Measured on 2026-08-08: a frame block ending "No split screen, no panels, no
  dividing lines ... no inset or corner vignette" produced an image with a
  drawn border inset from the edges. Told not to divide the frame, the model
  drew a single panel instead.

  Prohibitions belong in the negative prompt, which `build_image_prompt`
  assembles separately from `style.avoid`, `character.never` and the caller's
  `scene_negative`. Adding a "no ..." line here would undo that.
-#}
